Solution: Make a diagram. Two geometric figures intersect if they have one or more points in common. Draw two circles which intersect in $2$ points. Draw a line which intersects the two circles in $4$ points. Draw another line which intersects the two circles in $4$ points and also intersects the first line. There are $\boxed{11}$ points of intersection. [asy]

